## std/petitio.pengu — a high-level HTTP client with a `requests`-shaped API.
##
## `std.petitio` (Latin *petitio*, "a request") is PenguScript's HTTP client.
## It is a synchronous, explicit, `result`-returning wrapper over **libcurl**:
## GET/POST/PUT/DELETE/HEAD/PATCH/OPTIONS, custom headers, JSON and
## form-urlencoded bodies, multipart/form-data, query strings, URL parsing,
## total and connect timeouts, redirect control, TLS verification, Basic and
## Bearer authentication, proxies, per-response body caps, sessions with
## cookies, and a `Response` that can parse JSON.
##
## ## Why libcurl and not naett
##
## `naett` (single header, MIT) was evaluated first. Its public API cannot
## express what this module promises: `naettTimeout` is a *connect* timeout only,
## redirects are hard-wired on with no limit, there is no cookie control, no TLS
## toggle, no proxy, no multipart, and duplicate response headers (every
## `Set-Cookie` after the first) are lost. Its Linux backend is libcurl anyway, so
## it never removed the dependency — and the vendored copy did not compile under
## this repository's `-std=c99 -Wall -Wextra -Werror` gate. libcurl (`curl`
## licence, MIT-like) is preinstalled on Linux, macOS and every CI image used
## here, and exposes every knob documented below. See `docs/PETITIO.md`
## §"Why libcurl" for the full comparison.
##
## ## Quick start
## ```pengu
## import std.petitio
## import std.spark
##
## weave main into int:
##     var r as result of Response to HttpError is calling petitio.get with "https://httpbin.org/get"
##     defer banish r                       # the result owns the payload
##     if not r.is_ok:
##         var failure as HttpError is calling petitio.take_error with (sigil of r)
##         var why as string is calling failure.message
##         calling spark.println with why
##         banish why
##         banish failure
##         return 1
##     var resp as Response is calling petitio.take_response with (sigil of r)
##     defer banish resp
##     var body as string is calling resp.text
##     calling spark.println with body
##     banish body
##     calling spark.println_int with resp.status
##     return 0
## ```
##
## ## Ownership (read this once)
## - `Request` owns its URL, headers, body, auth strings and multipart parts.
##   `banish req` releases all of them (`Request derive Nexus`).
## - `Response` owns its body, URL, headers and cookies. `banish resp` releases
##   all of them, including every string inside the two maps.
## - `Session` owns its default headers and cookies. `banish session` releases
##   them.
## - A `result of Response to HttpError` owns its payload: `banish r` releases
##   the `Response` (or the `HttpError`) the box points at. `r.value` and
##   `r.error` hand out a **copy**, so releasing both the copy *and* the result
##   frees the same buffers twice. Either borrow through `r.value` / `r.error`
##   and release only the result (`defer banish r`), or move the payload out
##   with `take_response` / `take_error` and then release both independently.
##   Never `banish` a payload you obtained with `r.value` / `r.error`.
## - Every string getter (`Response.text`, `Response.header`, `HttpError.message`)
##   returns an **owned** copy. `banish` it when done. `Response.header` returns
##   `""` for an absent header; use `Response.has_header` when an empty header
##   value must be told apart from a missing one (a `maybe string` would wrap an
##   owned payload in a box the compiler cannot move out safely).
##
## ## Errors
## Every network operation returns `result ... to HttpError`; none of them
## panic on a transport failure. Malformed *program input* to a builder
## (`Request.new` with a method containing a space, `Request.header` with CR/LF
## or ':' in the name, `Request.set_cookie` with ';' in the value) is a bug in
## the caller and panics with a message naming the offending value — validate
## untrusted data before you build the request (§14.36 of the Pengunic guide).
## `multipart_file` is the exception: it reports `false` instead of panicking
## because a missing file is a runtime condition, not a bug.
##
## ## Feature matrix
## | Feature | Supported |
## |---|---|
## | GET / POST / PUT / DELETE / HEAD / PATCH / OPTIONS, custom methods | ✅ |
## | Request headers (case-insensitive, lower-cased in the maps) | ✅ |
## | JSON body (`json_body`) | ✅ |
## | form-urlencoded body (`form_body`) | ✅ |
## | multipart/form-data, in memory and from a file | ✅ |
## | Query strings (`build_query_string`, `with_query`) | ✅ |
## | URL parsing (`parse_url`) and percent-coding (`url_encode`/`url_decode`) | ✅ |
## | Total and connect timeouts | ✅ |
## | Redirect following with a limit, or none | ✅ |
## | TLS verification toggle (`insecure`) | ✅ |
## | Basic and Bearer authentication | ✅ |
## | Proxy (`proxy`) | ✅ |
## | Cookies (`Session`) | ✅ name/value, `Max-Age=0` deletion |
## | Response body cap (`max_body_bytes`) | ✅ |
## | Streaming downloads, connection pooling, HTTP/2 tuning, async | ❌ out of scope |
##
## ## Complexity
## | Operation | Cost |
## |---|---|
## | `Request.send` / `Session.request` | network-bound; body + headers copied once |
## | `url_encode` / `url_decode` | O(n) |
## | `build_query_string` | O(n log n) for n parameters (keys are sorted) |
## | `parse_url` | O(n) |
## | `Response.json` | O(body size) |
##
## ## Versioning
## `PETITIO_VERSION` follows the stdlib versioning policy (LANGUAGE.md §19.0):
## the stdlib release that ships this module.

import std.archivum
import std.builder
import std.chronicle
import std.compass
import std.ffi
import std.json
import std.scrolls
import std.spark

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Module version and tuning
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

## Petitio module version (the stdlib release that ships it).
const PETITIO_VERSION as string is "2.12.0"

## Redirect limit used by `Request.new` and by the one-shot helpers, matching
## Python's `requests`.
const PETITIO_DEFAULT_MAX_REDIRECTS as int is 30

## Default total timeout in seconds. `0.0` means "no deadline", like `requests`.
const PETITIO_DEFAULT_TIMEOUT_SEC as f64 is 0.0

## `User-Agent` sent when the request does not set one.
const PETITIO_DEFAULT_USER_AGENT as string is "petitio/2.12.0"

## Content type `json_body` installs when the request has not set one.
const PETITIO_JSON_CONTENT_TYPE as string is "application/json"

## Content type `form_body` installs when the request has not set one.
const PETITIO_FORM_CONTENT_TYPE as string is "application/x-www-form-urlencoded"

## Content type `multipart_file` installs when the part has none.
const PETITIO_BINARY_CONTENT_TYPE as string is "application/octet-stream"

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Error model
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

## Why an HTTP operation failed.
##
## ## Memoria
## Variants that carry a `string` own it (`HttpError derive Nexus`): extract the
## error from a result and `banish` it to release the message.
omen HttpError derive Nexus:
    ## DNS failure, a refused/reset connection, or a transfer interrupted
    ## mid-flight.
    ConnectionFailed with reason as string
    ## The total or connect deadline expired. `seconds` is the configured
    ## timeout, or the connect timeout when only that one was set.
    Timeout with seconds as f64
    ## The redirect limit was reached before a final response arrived.
    TooManyRedirects with count as int
    ## libcurl rejected the URL before any connection was attempted.
    InvalidUrl with url as string
    ## TLS negotiation, certificate or hostname verification failed.
    TlsError with reason as string
    ## A malformed response, a callback abort, or an option libcurl rejected.
    ProtocolError with reason as string
    ## The body exceeded the request's `max_body_bytes` cap.
    BodyTooLarge with max_bytes as i64
    ## An allocation failed.
    OutOfMemory
    ## The URL names a protocol other than HTTP or HTTPS.
    Unsupported with reason as string
    ## A local file could not be opened, written or read (streaming).
    IoError with reason as string
    ## A `send_stream` callback returned `false`, aborting the transfer.
    Cancelled
    ## `raise_for_status` saw a 4xx/5xx response. The response is still
    ## available; this variant carries only the status code.
    HttpStatus with status as int

enchanting HttpError:
    ## A human-readable description of the failure.
    ##
    ## ## Retorno
    ## An owned string with the variant and its payload, e.g.
    ## `"connection failed: Could not connect to server"`. `banish` it.
    ##
    ## ## Ejemplo
    ## ```pengu
    ## var e as HttpError is r.error
    ## calling spark.println with (calling e.message)
    ## banish e
    ## ```
    weave message into string:
        return judge (essence of self):
            when ConnectionFailed with reason -> "connection failed: {reason}"
            when Timeout with seconds -> "request timed out after {seconds}s"
            when TooManyRedirects with count -> "too many redirects (limit {count})"
            when InvalidUrl with url -> "invalid URL: {url}"
            when TlsError with reason -> "TLS error: {reason}"
            when ProtocolError with reason -> "protocol error: {reason}"
            when BodyTooLarge with max_bytes -> "response body exceeds {max_bytes} bytes"
            when OutOfMemory -> "out of memory"
            when Unsupported with reason -> "unsupported URL: {reason}"
            when IoError with reason -> "I/O error: {reason}"
            when Cancelled -> "transfer cancelled by callback"
            when HttpStatus with status -> "HTTP status {status}"

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Types
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

## One part of a `multipart/form-data` body.
##
## ## Memoria
## Owns all four strings; `banish part` releases them. A `Request` owns its
## parts, so `banish req` releases them through the derived `Nexus`.
rune FormPart derive Nexus:
    ## The form field name.
    name as string
    ## The part contents, byte-exact (a file's bytes or a text value).
    value as string
    ## The `filename` parameter, or `""` for a plain field.
    filename as string
    ## The part `Content-Type`, or `""` to let libcurl omit it.
    content_type as string

## The HTTP protocol version requested from the server.
##
## ## Memoria
## A plain C enum: no heap, nothing to release.
omen HttpVersion:
    ## HTTP/1.0, explicitly. Rarely what you want; HTTP/1.1 is the default.
    Http10
    ## HTTP/1.1 explicitly. The default, and what every server understands.
    Http11
    ## Negotiates HTTP/2 over ALPN and falls back to HTTP/1.1 when the server
    ## does not offer it. Requires libcurl built with HTTP/2 support (7.47+).
    Http2
    ## Forces HTTP/2 without negotiation ("prior knowledge"). Fails with a
    ## protocol error when the server only speaks HTTP/1.1.
    Http2PriorKnowledge
    ## HTTP/3. **Reported only** (`Response.http_version`): requesting it from a
    ## `Request` panics, because a reliable HTTP/3 client needs a libcurl built
    ## with QUIC support, which is not a portable assumption. A server may still
    ## negotiate it when the library supports it.
    Http3

## How a request authenticates with `basic_user` / `basic_password`.
##
## ## Memoria
## A plain C enum: no heap, nothing to release.
omen AuthMode:
    ## No authentication (the default).
    NoAuth
    ## HTTP Basic (RFC 7617): the credentials travel on every request.
    BasicAuth
    ## HTTP Digest (RFC 7616): libcurl answers the server's `401` challenge and
    ## retries with a hashed response. The password never crosses the wire.
    DigestAuth
    ## Negotiates: libcurl picks the strongest scheme the server offers
    ## (Digest when available, Basic otherwise).
    AnyAuth

## A configurable HTTP request.
##
## Build it with `Request.new`, mutate it with the builder methods, send it with
## `send`, then release it with `banish req`.
##
## ## Memoria
## `Request derive Nexus` releases `url`, `body`, `method`, every header key and
## value, the auth/proxy strings and every `FormPart` in `parts`.
rune Request derive Nexus:
    ## The HTTP method, upper-case (`"GET"`, `"POST"`, …). Custom verbs are
    ## allowed as long as they are RFC 7230 tokens.
    method as string
    ## The absolute URL, including `http://` or `https://`.
    url as string
    ## Request headers. Keys are stored lower-case; use `header` to set them.
    headers as map of string to string
    ## The request body. Empty unless `text_body`, `json_body`, `form_body` or
    ## `bytes_body` set it.
    body as string
    ## `true` when `body` is meant to be sent (an empty body is still a body).
    has_body as bool
    ## Total deadline in seconds; `0.0` disables it.
    timeout_sec as f64
    ## Connect deadline in seconds; `0.0` disables it (the total deadline still
    ## applies).
    connect_timeout_sec as f64
    ## Follow 3xx responses when `true`.
    follow_redirects as bool
    ## Maximum number of redirects to follow.
    max_redirects as int
    ## Verify the peer certificate and hostname when `true`. Disable only for
    ## testing against a self-signed endpoint.
    verify_tls as bool
    ## Protocol version to request. Set it with the `http_version` builder.
    http_version as HttpVersion
    ## Abort with `HttpError.BodyTooLarge` once the body exceeds this many
    ## bytes. `0` means unlimited.
    max_body_bytes as i64
    ## Authentication user name; empty disables authentication.
    basic_user as string
    ## Authentication password (ignored when `basic_user` is empty).
    basic_password as string
    ## Authentication scheme. Set it with `auth_basic`, `auth_digest` or
    ## `auth_any`; `NoAuth` (the default) sends no credentials.
    auth_mode as AuthMode
    ## Bearer token; empty disables it. An explicit `Authorization` header wins.
    bearer_token as string
    ## Proxy URL, e.g. `"http://127.0.0.1:8080"`; empty disables the proxy.
    proxy as string
    ## Proxy credentials as `"user:password"`, or empty.
    proxy_credentials as string
    ## `multipart/form-data` parts. When non-empty they replace `body`.
    parts as list of FormPart

## An HTTP response, as received (after redirects).
##
## ## Memoria
## `Response derive Nexus` releases `body`, `url`, every header key/value and
## every cookie key/value, plus the private list of cleared cookie names.
rune Response derive Nexus:
    ## The final HTTP status code (after redirects). `0` when no response line
    ## was received.
    status as int
    ## Final-response headers. Keys are lower-case; duplicate names keep the
    ## last value (use `cookies` for every `Set-Cookie`).
    headers as map of string to string
    ## The response body, byte-exact. Compressed responses are decoded by
    ## libcurl, so this is the plain payload.
    body as string
    ## The effective URL, after any redirects.
    url as string
    ## Wall-clock duration of the transfer, in seconds.
    elapsed_sec as f64
    ## Bytes the transfer wrote: the body length for an in-memory response, or
    ## the bytes written to the file / handed to the callback when streaming
    ## (`body` is empty in that case).
    bytes_written as i64
    ## The protocol the server actually spoke (`Http10`, `Http11`, `Http2` or
    ## `Http3`), as reported by libcurl. Requesting `Http2` does not guarantee
    ## the response used it; check this field.
    http_version as HttpVersion
    ## `true` when at least one redirect was followed.
    redirected as bool
    ## Cookies the server set, name → value, ignoring those it cleared.
    cookies as map of string to string
    ## Cookie names the server cleared with `Max-Age=0`. `Session` consumes the
    ## list to forget stale cookies; it is public so a hand-built `Response`
    ## (tests, fixtures) can set it.
    cleared_cookies as list of string

## A set of default headers and cookies applied to many requests, with cookie
## persistence.
##
## ## Memoria
## `Session derive Nexus` releases both maps and every string inside them.
rune Session derive Nexus:
    ## Headers applied to every request that does not set the same name.
    _default_headers as map of string to string
    ## Cookies applied to every request and updated from every response.
    _cookies as map of string to string

## The pieces of an absolute URL.
##
## ## Memoria
## Owns every field; `banish parts` releases them.
rune UrlParts derive Nexus:
    ## The scheme, as written (`"http"` or `"https"`).
    scheme as string
    ## `user:password`, or `""` when the URL carries no user info.
    userinfo as string
    ## The host, without brackets for an IPv6 literal.
    host as string
    ## The explicit port, or `0` when the URL omits it.
    port as int
    ## The path, `"/"` when the URL has none.
    path as string
    ## The query string without `?`, or `""`.
    query as string
    ## The fragment without `#`, or `""`.
    fragment as string

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Explicit moves out of a result
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# A `result` owns its payload: `banish r` releases the `Response` (or the
# `HttpError`) the box points at.  `r.value` and `r.error` hand out a *copy* of
# that payload, so banishing both the copy and the result frees the same
# buffers twice.  These two helpers move the payload out and clear the box, the
# same explicit-move contract `std.json` exposes as `take_value`/`take_string`.

## Moves the successful `Response` out of `r`, leaving `r` safe to `banish`.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `r`: a result. The box is consumed; `r.is_ok` becomes `false`.
##
## ## Retorno
## The owned `Response` (release it with `banish`). When `r` is an error, an
## empty `Response` is returned (status `0`, empty maps) and the error stays in
## the box for `banish r` to release.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## var r as result of Response to HttpError is calling petitio.get with url
## if not r.is_ok:
##     var e as HttpError is calling petitio.take_error with (sigil of r)
##     calling spark.println with (calling e.message)
##     banish e
##     banish r
##     return 1
## var resp as Response is calling petitio.take_response with (sigil of r)
## defer banish r
## defer banish resp
## ```
weave take_response with r as ref to result of Response to HttpError into Response:
    return calling _take_response with r

antiquus _take_response with r as ref to result of Response to HttpError into Response:
    r"""
if (r && r->is_ok && r->ok_val)
{
    Response out = *(Response *)r->ok_val;
    free(r->ok_val);
    r->ok_val = NULL;
    r->is_ok = false;
    return out;
}
Response empty;
memset(&empty, 0, sizeof empty);
return empty;
"""

## Moves the `HttpError` out of `r`, leaving `r` safe to `banish`.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `r`: a result. The box is consumed; `r` no longer carries the error.
##
## ## Retorno
## The owned `HttpError` (release it with `banish`). When `r` is `ok`, a
## placeholder error is returned whose `message` is meaningless; only call this
## after checking `r.is_ok`.
weave take_error shard T with r as ref to result of T to HttpError into HttpError:
    return calling _take_error with r

## The C half of `take_error` (see `_take_response` for the ownership why).
antiquus _take_error shard T with r as ref to result of T to HttpError into HttpError:
    r"""
if (r && !r->is_ok && r->err_val)
{
    HttpError out = *(HttpError *)r->err_val;
    free(r->err_val);
    r->err_val = NULL;
    return out;
}
/* No error to move.  The placeholder is tag 0 with an empty, non-owning reason
 * so that calling `message` on it cannot format a NULL pointer. */
HttpError empty;
memset(&empty, 0, sizeof empty);
empty.data.ConnectionFailed.reason = pengu_string_from_cstr("");
return empty;
"""

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Byte-level helpers
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

## An owned copy of `s` (one allocation). The caller `banish`es it.
weave _copy with s as string into string:
    return calling scrolls.substring with s, 0, (s length)

## The ASCII lower-case byte of `b`; every other byte is returned unchanged.
weave _lower_byte with b as int into int:
    if b >= 65 and b <= 90:
        return b + 32
    return b

## `true` when `b` is an RFC 7230 token byte (`tchar`).
weave _is_token_byte with b as int into bool:
    if b >= 48 and b <= 57:
        return true
    if b >= 65 and b <= 90:
        return true
    if b >= 97 and b <= 122:
        return true
    if b == 33 or b == 35 or b == 36 or b == 37 or b == 38 or b == 39:
        return true
    if b == 42 or b == 43 or b == 45 or b == 46:
        return true
    if b == 94 or b == 95 or b == 96 or b == 124 or b == 126:
        return true
    return false

## `true` when `s` is a non-empty RFC 7230 token (used for methods, header
## names and cookie names).
weave _is_token with s as string into bool:
    var n as int is s length
    if n == 0:
        return false
    var raw as ref to frozen byte is bytes of s
    var i as int is 0
    while i < n:
        if not calling _is_token_byte with ((raw at i) to int):
            return false
        set i is i + 1
    return true

## `true` when `s` contains a byte that would corrupt a header or cookie line:
## CR, LF or NUL.
##
## CR/LF would inject a second line; NUL truncates the value when the C bridge
## copies it into libcurl's NUL-terminated header list, silently changing the
## request. Both are rejected before they reach the wire.
weave _has_control_byte with s as string into bool:
    var raw as ref to frozen byte is bytes of s
    var i as int is 0
    var n as int is s length
    while i < n:
        var b as int is (raw at i) to int
        if b == 10 or b == 13 or b == 0:
            return true
        set i is i + 1
    return false

## The byte offset of the first case-insensitive occurrence of `needle` in
## `haystack`, or `-1`.
##
## Used for `Set-Cookie` attribute names, which are case-insensitive while the
## *values* (dates, paths) must keep their original case for `curl_getdate`.
weave _find_ci with haystack as string, needle as string into int:
    var hn as int is haystack length
    var nn as int is needle length
    if nn == 0:
        return 0
    if nn > hn:
        return -1
    var hay as ref to frozen byte is bytes of haystack
    var pin as ref to frozen byte is bytes of needle
    var i as int is 0
    while i + nn <= hn:
        var j as int is 0
        var same as bool is true
        while j < nn:
            if (calling _lower_byte with ((hay at (i + j)) to int)) != (calling _lower_byte with ((pin at j) to int)):
                set same is false
                break
            set j is j + 1
        if same:
            return i
        set i is i + 1
    return -1

## `true` when `b` may appear unescaped in a percent-encoded string
## (RFC 3986 `unreserved`: `A-Z a-z 0-9 - . _ ~`).
weave _is_unreserved with b as int into bool:
    if b >= 48 and b <= 57:
        return true
    if b >= 65 and b <= 90:
        return true
    if b >= 97 and b <= 122:
        return true
    return b == 45 or b == 46 or b == 95 or b == 126

## The value of one upper-case hex digit.
weave _hex_digit with nibble as int into char:
    if nibble < 10:
        return ((48 + nibble) to char)
    return ((55 + nibble) to char)

## The numeric value of a hex digit, or -1 when `b` is not one.
weave _hex_value with b as int into int:
    if b >= 48 and b <= 57:
        return b - 48
    if b >= 65 and b <= 70:
        return b - 55
    if b >= 97 and b <= 102:
        return b - 87
    return -1

## Converts a non-negative seconds value to whole milliseconds.
weave _seconds_to_ms with seconds as f64 into i64:
    if seconds <= 0.0:
        return 0
    return ((seconds * 1000.0) + 0.5) to i64

## `1` for `true`, `0` for `false`.
weave _flag with value as bool into int:
    if value:
        return 1
    return 0

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Owned map helpers
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

## Inserts `key` → `value` into `m`, taking ownership of both.
##
## ## Memoria
## The map copies the `PenguString` headers and adopts the buffers. When the key
## already exists, the old value and the old key buffer are released and the new
## pair is inserted at a fresh slot: overwriting in place would drop the old
## value's buffer (`pengu_map_put` never frees it) and passing a map-owned key
## back to `put` is unsafe across a rehash.
##
## ## Invariante de iteración
## `m.remove` only tomb-stones the slot (it never grows or rehashes the table),
## and the `put` that can rehash runs **after** the loop has exited, so mutating
## the map from inside the `for` cannot invalidate the iterator. The loop breaks
## immediately after the match for the same reason.
weave _put_owned with m as ref to map of string to string, key as string, value as string into void:
    for existing in essence of m:
        if (calling scrolls.compare with existing, key) == 0:
            var old_value as string is calling m.get with existing
            var old_key as string is existing
            calling m.remove with existing
            banish old_value
            banish old_key
            break
    calling m.put with key, value

## Removes `key` from `m` and releases the stored key and value.
##
## ## Retorno
## `true` when the key was present.
weave _remove_owned with m as ref to map of string to string, key as string into bool:
    for existing in essence of m:
        if (calling scrolls.compare with existing, key) == 0:
            var old_value as string is calling m.get with existing
            var old_key as string is existing
            calling m.remove with existing
            banish old_value
            banish old_key
            return true
    return false

## `true` when `m` has `key` (exact byte match; header keys are lower-case).
weave _has_key with m as ref to map of string to string, key as string into bool:
    return calling m.contains with key

## Validates `name`/`value` and stores them in `m` under a lower-case key.
##
## ## Panics
## When `name` is not an RFC 7230 token, or `name`/`value` contains CR or LF.
## A header that could inject a second header line is a bug in the caller, never
## a network condition.
weave _set_header with m as ref to map of string to string, name as string, value as string into void:
    if not calling _is_token with name:
        calling spark.panic with "petitio: invalid header name '{name}': expected an RFC 7230 token"
    if calling _has_control_byte with value:
        calling spark.panic with "petitio: header '{name}' value contains CR, LF or NUL (header injection)"
    var key as string is calling scrolls.lower with name
    var stored as string is calling _copy with value
    calling _put_owned with m, key, stored

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Request construction
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

enchanting Request:
    ## Creates a request with every default filled in.
    ##
    ## ## Parámetros
    ## - `method`: the HTTP method. Token-validated and upper-cased.
    ## - `url`: the absolute URL. Copied; the caller keeps its string.
    ##
    ## ## Retorno
    ## A fresh `Request`: follows up to `PETITIO_DEFAULT_MAX_REDIRECTS`
    ## redirects, verifies TLS, has no timeout and no body.
    ##
    ## ## Panics
    ## When `method` is not an RFC 7230 token.
    ##
    ## ## Ejemplo
    ## ```pengu
    ## var req as Request is calling Request.new with "POST", "https://api.example.com/items"
    ## defer banish req
    ## calling req.header with "Accept", "application/json"
    ## ```
    weave ritual new with method as string, url as string into Request:
        if not calling _is_token with method:
            calling spark.panic with "petitio: invalid HTTP method '{method}'"
        var headers as map of string to string is map of string to string
        var parts as list of FormPart is list of FormPart
        var request as Request is:
            method is (calling scrolls.upper with method)
            url is (calling _copy with url)
            headers is headers
            body is ""
            has_body is false
            timeout_sec is PETITIO_DEFAULT_TIMEOUT_SEC
            connect_timeout_sec is 0.0
            follow_redirects is true
            max_redirects is PETITIO_DEFAULT_MAX_REDIRECTS
            verify_tls is true
            http_version is HttpVersion.Http11
            max_body_bytes is 0
            basic_user is ""
            basic_password is ""
            auth_mode is AuthMode.NoAuth
            bearer_token is ""
            proxy is ""
            proxy_credentials is ""
            parts is parts
        return request

    ## Sets a request header, replacing any previous value for that name.
    ##
    ## Header names are case-insensitive: `Content-Type` and `content-type` are
    ## the same header, stored under the lower-case spelling.
    ##
    ## ## Panics
    ## When the name is not an RFC 7230 token, or either part contains CR/LF.
    weave header with name as string, value as string into void:
        calling _set_header with (sigil of self->headers), name, value

    ## Removes a request header. Returns `true` when it was present.
    weave remove_header with name as string into bool:
        var key as string is calling scrolls.lower with name
        var removed as bool is calling _remove_owned with (sigil of self->headers), key
        banish key
        return removed

    ## `true` when the request sets `name` (case-insensitive).
    weave has_header with name as string into bool:
        var key as string is calling scrolls.lower with name
        var present as bool is calling _has_key with (sigil of self->headers), key
        banish key
        return present

    ## Sets a plain text body.
    ##
    ## The body is sent as-is; no `Content-Type` is added. Use `json_body` or
    ## `form_body` when the payload needs one.
    weave text_body with s as string into void:
        var old as string is self->body
        banish old
        set self->body is (calling _copy with s)
        set self->has_body is true

    ## Serializes `v` as JSON and installs it as the body plus
    ## `Content-Type: application/json`.
    ##
    ## The content type is always set, so call `header` **after** this method to
    ## use a vendor media type (`application/vnd.api+json`, …).
    ##
    ## ## Ejemplo
    ## ```pengu
    ## var obj as JsonValue is calling JsonValue.object
    ## calling obj.put_string with "name", "pengu"
    ## calling req.json_body with obj
    ## banish obj
    ## ```
    weave json_body with v as json.JsonValue into void:
        var text as string is calling json.stringify with v
        calling self.text_body with text
        banish text
        calling self.header with "Content-Type", PETITIO_JSON_CONTENT_TYPE

    ## Encodes `fields` as `application/x-www-form-urlencoded` and installs the
    ## result as the body plus the matching `Content-Type`.
    ##
    ## Like `json_body`, the content type is always set; call `header` afterwards
    ## to override it.
    weave form_body with fields as map of string to string into void:
        var encoded as string is calling build_query_string with fields
        calling self.text_body with encoded
        banish encoded
        calling self.header with "Content-Type", PETITIO_FORM_CONTENT_TYPE

    ## Sets a byte-exact body (binary data is allowed).
    weave bytes_body with data as string into void:
        calling self.text_body with data

    ## Sets the total deadline, in seconds. `0.0` disables it.
    weave timeout with seconds as f64 into void:
        set self->timeout_sec is seconds
        if seconds < 0.0:
            set self->timeout_sec is 0.0

    ## Sets the connect deadline, in seconds. `0.0` disables it.
    weave connect_timeout with seconds as f64 into void:
        set self->connect_timeout_sec is seconds
        if seconds < 0.0:
            set self->connect_timeout_sec is 0.0

    ## Stops at the first 3xx response instead of following it.
    weave no_redirects into void:
        set self->follow_redirects is false

    ## Follows redirects, up to `count`. `count` must be positive.
    weave max_redirects with count as int into void:
        if count <= 0:
            calling spark.panic with "petitio: max_redirects expects a positive count"
        set self->follow_redirects is true
        set self->max_redirects is count

    ## Disables TLS certificate and hostname verification.
    ##
    ## ## Advertencia
    ## This makes the connection trivially interceptable. Use it only against a
    ## test endpoint you control.
    weave insecure into void:
        set self->verify_tls is false

    ## Requests a specific HTTP protocol version.
    ##
    ## ## Parámetros
    ## - `version`: `Http11` (default), `Http2` (ALPN negotiation, falls back to
    ##   HTTP/1.1) or `Http2PriorKnowledge` (force HTTP/2, no fallback).
    ##
    ## ## Ejemplo
    ## ```pengu
    ## calling req.http_version with HttpVersion.Http2
    ## ```
    weave http_version with version as HttpVersion into void:
        if version == HttpVersion.Http3:
            calling spark.panic with "petitio: HTTP/3 cannot be requested; libcurl may still negotiate it (check Response.http_version)"
        set self->http_version is version

    ## Sends HTTP Basic credentials (RFC 7617).
    ##
    ## ## Advertencia
    ## Basic sends the password on every request; over plain HTTP that is
    ## readable by anyone on the path. Use HTTPS.
    weave auth_basic with user as string, password as string into void:
        banish self->basic_user
        banish self->basic_password
        set self->basic_user is (calling _copy with user)
        set self->basic_password is (calling _copy with password)
        set self->auth_mode is AuthMode.BasicAuth

    ## Sends HTTP Digest credentials (RFC 7616).
    ##
    ## libcurl answers the server's `401` challenge and retries with a hashed
    ## response, so the password never crosses the wire. The server must offer
    ## Digest; if it does not, the request fails with the server's `401` status.
    ##
    ## ## Advertencia
    ## Digest over plain HTTP still lets an attacker capture and replay the
    ## exchange. Use HTTPS.
    weave auth_digest with user as string, password as string into void:
        banish self->basic_user
        banish self->basic_password
        set self->basic_user is (calling _copy with user)
        set self->basic_password is (calling _copy with password)
        set self->auth_mode is AuthMode.DigestAuth

    ## Negotiates the authentication scheme with the server.
    ##
    ## libcurl uses the strongest scheme the server offers (Digest when
    ## available, Basic otherwise).
    weave auth_any with user as string, password as string into void:
        banish self->basic_user
        banish self->basic_password
        set self->basic_user is (calling _copy with user)
        set self->basic_password is (calling _copy with password)
        set self->auth_mode is AuthMode.AnyAuth

    ## Sends `Authorization: Bearer <token>`.
    ##
    ## An `Authorization` header set explicitly with `header` wins.
    weave auth_bearer with token as string into void:
        banish self->bearer_token
        set self->bearer_token is (calling _copy with token)

    ## Routes the request through a SOCKS5 proxy, resolving DNS **on the proxy**.
    ##
    ## Equivalent to `proxy("socks5h://" + url, credentials)`. The `h` matters:
    ## `socks5h` sends the host name to the proxy instead of resolving it
    ## locally, so the proxy (not your machine) sees the destination and no DNS
    ## query leaks. A URL that already carries a scheme (`socks5://`,
    ## `socks5h://`, `http://`) is used as given.
    ##
    ## ## Parámetros
    ## - `url`: `"host:port"` (for example `"127.0.0.1:1080"`).
    ## - `credentials`: `"user:password"`, or `""` for an open proxy.
    ##
    ## ## Ejemplo
    ## ```pengu
    ## calling req.socks_proxy with "127.0.0.1:1080", ""
    ## ```
    weave socks_proxy with url as string, credentials as string into void:
        if calling scrolls.contains with url, "://":
            calling self.proxy with url, credentials
            return
        var full as string is "socks5h://{url}"
        calling self.proxy with full, credentials
        banish full

    ## Routes the request through `proxy` (`"http://host:port"`), optionally
    ## authenticated with `"user:password"`.
    weave proxy with proxy as string, credentials as string into void:
        banish self->proxy
        banish self->proxy_credentials
        set self->proxy is (calling _copy with proxy)
        set self->proxy_credentials is (calling _copy with credentials)

    ## Caps the response body. Exceeding it fails with
    ## `HttpError.BodyTooLarge` and the transfer is aborted.
    weave max_body_bytes with limit as i64 into void:
        if limit < 0:
            set self->max_body_bytes is 0
        else:
            set self->max_body_bytes is limit

    ## Adds a `multipart/form-data` text field.
    weave multipart_field with name as string, value as string into void:
        calling self.multipart_bytes with name, value, "", ""

    ## Adds a `multipart/form-data` part with explicit file name and type.
    ##
    ## ## Parámetros
    ## - `name`: the form field name.
    ## - `data`: the part bytes (copied; binary is allowed).
    ## - `filename`: the `filename` parameter, or `""` for none.
    ## - `content_type`: the part type, or `""` to let libcurl omit it.
    weave multipart_bytes with name as string, data as string, filename as string, content_type as string into void:
        if not calling _is_token with name:
            calling spark.panic with "petitio: invalid multipart field name '{name}'"
        var part as FormPart is:
            name is (calling _copy with name)
            value is (calling _copy with data)
            filename is (calling _copy with filename)
            content_type is (calling _copy with content_type)
        calling self->parts.push with part

    ## Adds a file as a `multipart/form-data` part, read into memory now.
    ##
    ## ## Retorno
    ## `true` when the file was read and the part added; `false` when `path`
    ## could not be read (a runtime condition, so it does not panic).
    ##
    ## ## Memoria
    ## The file contents are copied into the request; the file handle is closed
    ## by `std.archivum` before this returns.
    weave multipart_file with name as string, path as string into bool:
        var content as maybe string is calling archivum.read_bytes with path
        if not content.is_present:
            banish content
            return false
        var data as string is content.value
        var filename as string is calling compass.basename with path
        calling self.multipart_bytes with name, data, filename, PETITIO_BINARY_CONTENT_TYPE
        banish filename
        banish data
        banish content
        return true

    ## Sends the request and waits for the response.
    ##
    ## ## Retorno
    ## `ok Response` (owned; `banish` it) or `err HttpError`. The request stays
    ## usable and can be sent again.
    ##
    ## ## Ejemplo
    ## ```pengu
    ## var r as result of Response to HttpError is calling req.send
    ## defer banish r
    ## if not r.is_ok:
    ##     return 1
    ## var resp as Response is r.value          # borrowed copy: do not banish
    ## calling spark.println_int with resp.status
    ## ```
    weave send into result of Response to HttpError:
        var no_defaults as map of string to string is map of string to string
        var no_cookies as map of string to string is map of string to string
        var outcome as result of Response to HttpError is calling _perform with self, (sigil of no_defaults), (sigil of no_cookies)
        banish no_defaults
        banish no_cookies
        return outcome

    ## Sends the request and writes the body to `path`, without buffering it.
    ##
    ## ## Parámetros
    ## - `path`: destination file, overwritten when it exists. Its parent
    ##   directory must exist.
    ##
    ## ## Retorno
    ## `ok Response` with `body == ""` and `bytes_written` set, or
    ## `err HttpError.IoError` when the file cannot be opened or written and
    ## `err HttpError.BodyTooLarge` when `max_body_bytes` is exceeded.
    ##
    ## ## Memoria
    ## The `Response` is owned; the `Request` stays reusable. The file is closed
    ## before this returns.
    ##
    ## ## Ejemplo
    ## ```pengu
    ## var req as Request is calling Request.new with "GET", "https://example.com/big.bin"
    ## calling req.max_body_bytes with 128 * 1024 * 1024
    ## var r as result of Response to HttpError is calling req.send_to_file with "big.bin"
    ## defer banish r
    ## ```
    weave send_to_file with path as string into result of Response to HttpError:
        var no_defaults as map of string to string is map of string to string
        var no_cookies as map of string to string is map of string to string
        var handle as ref to petitio_request is calling _build_handle with self, (sigil of no_defaults), (sigil of no_cookies)
        banish no_defaults
        banish no_cookies
        if calling ffi.is_null with handle:
            return calling err_of with (with OutOfMemory is 0)
        defer calling petitio_request_free with handle

        var raw as ref to petitio_response is calling petitio_request_perform_to_file with handle, path
        if calling ffi.is_null with raw:
            return calling err_of with (with OutOfMemory is 0)
        defer calling petitio_response_free with raw

        var code as int is calling petitio_response_error with raw
        if code != 0:
            var reason as string is calling petitio_response_error_message with raw
            var failure as HttpError is calling _error_from_code with code, reason, self
            banish reason
            return calling err_of with failure
        var response as Response is calling _response_from_c with raw, self
        return calling ok_of with response

    ## Sends the request and hands every body chunk to `cb`.
    ##
    ## ## Parámetros
    ## - `cb`: `weave chunk as string, user as ref to void into bool`. Return
    ##   `true` to continue, `false` to abort (`err HttpError.Cancelled`).
    ## - `user`: opaque context forwarded to `cb` (a `sigil of` a local is the
    ##   usual choice).
    ##
    ## ## Advertencia
    ## `chunk` is a **borrowed view** of libcurl's buffer. It is valid only
    ## during the call: do not store it, do not `banish` it and do not let it
    ## escape into a `defer`.
    ##
    ## ## Retorno
    ## `ok Response` with `body == ""` and `bytes_written` set, `err Cancelled`
    ## when `cb` returned `false`, or the usual transport errors.
    ##
    ## ## Ejemplo
    ## ```pengu
    ## weave count with chunk as string, user as ref to void into bool:
    ##     var total as ref to i64 is transmute user to ref to i64
    ##     set essence of total is (essence of total) + (chunk length to i64)
    ##     return true
    ##
    ## var total as i64 is 0
    ## var r as result of Response to HttpError is calling req.send_stream with count, (sigil of total)
    ## ```
    weave send_stream with cb as ref to weave with chunk as string, user as ref to void into bool, user as ref to void into result of Response to HttpError:
        var no_defaults as map of string to string is map of string to string
        var no_cookies as map of string to string is map of string to string
        var handle as ref to petitio_request is calling _build_handle with self, (sigil of no_defaults), (sigil of no_cookies)
        banish no_defaults
        banish no_cookies
        if calling ffi.is_null with handle:
            return calling err_of with (with OutOfMemory is 0)
        defer calling petitio_request_free with handle

        var raw as ref to petitio_response is calling petitio_request_perform_stream with handle, cb, user
        if calling ffi.is_null with raw:
            return calling err_of with (with OutOfMemory is 0)
        defer calling petitio_response_free with raw

        var code as int is calling petitio_response_error with raw
        if code != 0:
            var reason as string is calling petitio_response_error_message with raw
            var failure as HttpError is calling _error_from_code with code, reason, self
            banish reason
            return calling err_of with failure
        var response as Response is calling _response_from_c with raw, self
        return calling ok_of with response

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Response queries
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

enchanting Response:
    ## `true` for a 2xx status.
    weave is_ok into bool:
        return self->status >= 200 and self->status < 300

    ## `true` for a 3xx status (only observable with `no_redirects`).
    weave is_redirect into bool:
        return self->status >= 300 and self->status < 400

    ## `true` for a 4xx status.
    weave is_client_error into bool:
        return self->status >= 400 and self->status < 500

    ## `true` for a 5xx status.
    weave is_server_error into bool:
        return self->status >= 500 and self->status < 600

    ## An owned copy of the body.
    ##
    ## ## Memoria
    ## One allocation; `banish` it. `Response.body` is the same bytes without a
    ## copy.
    weave text into string:
        return calling _copy with self->body

    ## Parses the body as JSON.
    ##
    ## ## Retorno
    ## `ok JsonValue` (owned) or the parser's `JsonError`.
    weave json into result of json.JsonValue to json.JsonError:
        return calling json.parse with self->body

    ## One response header as an owned copy, or `""` when absent.
    ##
    ## ## Parámetros
    ## - `name`: the header name, compared case-insensitively.
    ##
    ## ## Retorno
    ## An owned string (an empty, non-owning `""` when the header is absent).
    ## Release it with `banish`; the empty case is a safe no-op.
    ##
    ## ## Ejemplo
    ## ```pengu
    ## var ctype as string is calling resp.header with "content-type"
    ## defer banish ctype
    ## if (calling resp.has_header with "content-type") and (ctype length) == 0:
    ##     calling spark.println with "the server sent an empty content-type"
    ## ```
    weave header with name as string into string:
        var key as string is calling scrolls.lower with name
        if not (calling self->headers.contains with key):
            banish key
            return ""
        var value as string is calling self->headers.get with key
        banish key
        return calling _copy with value

    ## `true` when the response carries header `name` (case-insensitive).
    weave has_header with name as string into bool:
        var key as string is calling scrolls.lower with name
        var present as bool is calling self->headers.contains with key
        banish key
        return present

    ## Fails with `HttpError.HttpStatus` when the status is 4xx or 5xx.
    ##
    ## ## Retorno
    ## `ok 0`, or `err HttpStatus`.
    weave raise_for_status into result of void to HttpError:
        if self->status >= 400:
            return calling err_of with (with HttpStatus is self->status)
        return calling ok_of with 0

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# URL helpers
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

## Percent-encodes `s` for use in a URL path or query value.
##
## Every byte outside RFC 3986's `unreserved` set (`A-Z a-z 0-9 - . _ ~`) becomes
## `%XX` with upper-case hex digits. Space becomes `%20`, never `+`, so the
## result round-trips through `url_decode`.
##
## ## Memoria
## Returns an owned string; `banish` it.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## var q as string is calling petitio.url_encode with "a b&c"
## defer banish q                     # "a%20b%26c"
## ```
weave url_encode with s as string into string:
    var raw as ref to frozen byte is bytes of s
    var n as int is s length
    var sb as StringBuilder is calling StringBuilder.new
    var i as int is 0
    while i < n:
        var b as int is (raw at i) to int
        if calling _is_unreserved with b:
            calling sb.append_char with (b to char)
        else:
            calling sb.append_char with (37 to char)
            calling sb.append_char with (calling _hex_digit with (b / 16))
            calling sb.append_char with (calling _hex_digit with (b % 16))
        set i is i + 1
    var out as string is calling sb.finish
    banish sb
    return out

## Decodes every `%XX` sequence in `s`.
##
## `+` is left as `+` (it is only a space in `application/x-www-form-urlencoded`,
## not in a URL). A malformed or truncated escape is copied verbatim, so decoding
## never fails and never loses bytes.
##
## ## Memoria
## Returns an owned string; `banish` it.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## var t as string is calling petitio.url_decode with "a%20b%26c"   # "a b&c"
## defer banish t
## ```
weave url_decode with s as string into string:
    var raw as ref to frozen byte is bytes of s
    var n as int is s length
    var sb as StringBuilder is calling StringBuilder.new
    var i as int is 0
    while i < n:
        var b as int is (raw at i) to int
        if b == 37 and i + 2 < n:
            var hi as int is calling _hex_value with ((raw at (i + 1)) to int)
            var lo as int is calling _hex_value with ((raw at (i + 2)) to int)
            if hi >= 0 and lo >= 0:
                calling sb.append_char with (((hi * 16) + lo) to char)
                set i is i + 3
            else:
                calling sb.append_char with (b to char)
                set i is i + 1
        else:
            calling sb.append_char with (b to char)
            set i is i + 1
    var out as string is calling sb.finish
    banish sb
    return out

## Builds `key=value&...` with both sides percent-encoded.
##
## Keys are sorted byte-wise first, so the same map always yields the same
## query string — the property cache keys and request signatures need. The
## leading `?` is **not** included.
##
## ## Memoria
## Returns an owned string; `banish` it.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## var params as map of string to string is map of string to string
## calling params.put with "q", "pengu script"
## var qs as string is calling petitio.build_query_string with params
## defer banish qs                    # "q=pengu%20script"
## banish params
## ```
weave build_query_string with params as map of string to string into string:
    var keys as list of string is list of string
    for k in params:
        calling keys.push with k
    var i as int is 0
    var n as int is keys.len
    while i < n:
        var j as int is i + 1
        while j < n:
            if (calling scrolls.compare with (keys at i), (keys at j)) > 0:
                var tmp as string is keys at i
                set keys at i is (keys at j)
                set keys at j is tmp
            set j is j + 1
        set i is i + 1
    var sb as StringBuilder is calling StringBuilder.new
    set i is 0
    while i < n:
        var key as string is keys at i
        if i > 0:
            calling sb.append_char with '&'
        var encoded_key as string is calling url_encode with key
        calling sb.append with encoded_key
        banish encoded_key
        calling sb.append_char with '='
        var value as string is calling params.get with key
        var encoded_value as string is calling url_encode with value
        calling sb.append with encoded_value
        banish encoded_value
        set i is i + 1
    var out as string is calling sb.finish
    banish sb
    banish keys
    return out

## Appends `params` to `url`, using `?` or `&` as needed.
##
## ## Memoria
## Returns an owned string; `banish` it.
weave with_query with url as string, params as map of string to string into string:
    if params.len == 0:
        return calling _copy with url
    var query as string is calling build_query_string with params
    var sb as StringBuilder is calling StringBuilder.new
    calling sb.append with url
    if (calling scrolls.contains with url, "?"):
        calling sb.append_char with '&'
    else:
        calling sb.append_char with '?'
    calling sb.append with query
    var out as string is calling sb.finish
    banish sb
    banish query
    return out

## Splits an absolute `http`/`https` URL into its parts.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `url`: an absolute URL. IPv6 hosts may be bracketed (`[::1]:8080`).
##
## ## Retorno
## `ok UrlParts` (owned; `banish` it) or `err message` describing the first
## structural problem (a borrowed literal, so nothing to release).
##
## ## Detalles
## The default port is **not** filled in: `port` is `0` when the URL omits it.
## The query is returned without `?` and the fragment without `#`. The path is
## `"/"` when the URL has none.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## var parsed as result of UrlParts to string is calling petitio.parse_url with "https://example.com:8443/a?b=1#c"
## defer banish parsed                       # owns the UrlParts payload
## if not parsed.is_ok:
##     return 1
## var parts as UrlParts is parsed.value     # borrowed copy: do not banish
## calling spark.println with parts.host      # example.com
## calling spark.println_int with parts.port  # 8443
## ```
weave parse_url with url as string into result of UrlParts to string:
    var n as int is url length
    if n == 0:
        return calling err_of with "empty URL"
    var raw as ref to frozen byte is bytes of url

    # scheme "://"
    var scheme_end as int is 0
    while scheme_end < n and (raw at scheme_end) != 58:
        set scheme_end is scheme_end + 1
    if scheme_end == 0 or scheme_end + 2 >= n:
        return calling err_of with "missing '://' after the scheme"
    if (raw at (scheme_end + 1)) != 47 or (raw at (scheme_end + 2)) != 47:
        return calling err_of with "missing '://' after the scheme"

    var authority_start as int is scheme_end + 3
    var authority_end as int is authority_start
    while authority_end < n and (raw at authority_end) != 47 and (raw at authority_end) != 63 and (raw at authority_end) != 35:
        set authority_end is authority_end + 1

    # userinfo: everything before the last '@'
    var at_pos as int is -1
    var scan as int is authority_start
    while scan < authority_end:
        if (raw at scan) == 64:
            set at_pos is scan
        set scan is scan + 1
    var host_start as int is authority_start
    if at_pos >= 0:
        set host_start is at_pos + 1

    # host and optional port
    var host_end as int is authority_end
    var port as int is 0
    var port_start as int is -1
    if host_start < authority_end and (raw at host_start) == 91:
        var close as int is host_start
        while close < authority_end and (raw at close) != 93:
            set close is close + 1
        if close >= authority_end:
            return calling err_of with "unterminated IPv6 literal"
        set host_end is close + 1
        if host_end < authority_end and (raw at host_end) == 58:
            set port_start is host_end + 1
    else:
        var colon as int is -1
        set scan is host_start
        while scan < authority_end:
            if (raw at scan) == 58:
                set colon is scan
            set scan is scan + 1
        if colon >= 0:
            set host_end is colon
            set port_start is colon + 1
    if port_start >= 0:
        if port_start >= authority_end:
            return calling err_of with "empty port"
        set scan is port_start
        while scan < authority_end:
            var digit as int is (raw at scan) to int
            if digit < 48 or digit > 57:
                return calling err_of with "port is not a decimal number"
            set port is (port * 10) + (digit - 48)
            if port > 65535:
                return calling err_of with "port is out of range"
            set scan is scan + 1
    if host_end <= host_start:
        return calling err_of with "missing host"

    # path, query, fragment
    var path_start as int is authority_end
    var path_end as int is authority_end
    while path_end < n and (raw at path_end) != 63 and (raw at path_end) != 35:
        set path_end is path_end + 1
    var query_start as int is -1
    var query_end as int is -1
    var fragment_start as int is -1
    if path_end < n and (raw at path_end) == 63:
        set query_start is path_end + 1
        set query_end is query_start
        while query_end < n and (raw at query_end) != 35:
            set query_end is query_end + 1
        set fragment_start is query_end
    else:
        set fragment_start is path_end

    var scheme as string is calling scrolls.substring with url, 0, scheme_end
    var userinfo as string is ""
    if at_pos >= 0:
        set userinfo is (calling scrolls.substring with url, authority_start, at_pos)
    var host as string is calling scrolls.substring with url, host_start, host_end
    var path as string is calling scrolls.substring with url, path_start, path_end
    if (path length) == 0:
        banish path
        set path is "/"
    var query as string is ""
    if query_start >= 0:
        set query is (calling scrolls.substring with url, query_start, query_end)
    var fragment as string is ""
    if fragment_start >= 0 and fragment_start < n:
        var frag_begin as int is fragment_start
        if frag_begin < n and (raw at frag_begin) == 35:
            set frag_begin is frag_begin + 1
        if frag_begin <= n:
            set fragment is (calling scrolls.substring with url, frag_begin, n)
    var parts as UrlParts is:
        scheme is scheme
        userinfo is userinfo
        host is host
        port is port
        path is path
        query is query
        fragment is fragment
    return calling ok_of with parts

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Transport: the one place that touches the C bridge
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

## Maps a `PETITIO_*` code to the matching `HttpError` variant.
weave _error_from_code with code as int, reason as string, request as ref to Request into HttpError:
    if code == 1:
        return with ConnectionFailed is (calling _copy with reason)
    if code == 2:
        var configured as f64 is request->timeout_sec
        if configured <= 0.0:
            set configured is request->connect_timeout_sec
        return with Timeout is configured
    if code == 3:
        return with TooManyRedirects is request->max_redirects
    if code == 4:
        return with InvalidUrl is (calling _copy with request->url)
    if code == 5:
        return with TlsError is (calling _copy with reason)
    if code == 7:
        return with BodyTooLarge is request->max_body_bytes
    if code == 8:
        return with OutOfMemory is 0
    if code == 9:
        return with Unsupported is (calling _copy with reason)
    if code == 10:
        return with IoError is (calling _copy with reason)
    if code == 11:
        return Cancelled
    return with ProtocolError is (calling _copy with reason)

## Copies the fields of a C response into an owned `Response`.
weave _response_from_c with raw as ref to petitio_response, request as ref to Request into Response:
    var headers as map of string to string is map of string to string
    var cookies as map of string to string is map of string to string
    var expired as list of string is list of string
    var count as int is calling petitio_response_header_count with raw
    var i as int is 0
    while i < count:
        var name as string is calling petitio_response_header_name with raw, i
        var value as string is calling petitio_response_header_value with raw, i
        if (calling scrolls.compare with name, "set-cookie") == 0:
            var cookie_name as string is calling _cookie_name with value
            var cookie_value as string is calling _cookie_value with value
            if (cookie_name length) > 0:
                if calling _cookie_cleared with value:
                    calling expired.push with cookie_name
                    banish cookie_value
                else:
                    calling _put_owned with (sigil of cookies), cookie_name, cookie_value
            else:
                banish cookie_name
                banish cookie_value
        calling _put_owned with (sigil of headers), name, value
        set i is i + 1
    var body as string is calling petitio_response_body with raw
    var effective as string is calling petitio_response_url with raw
    if (effective length) == 0:
        banish effective
        set effective is (calling _copy with request->url)
    var status as int is calling petitio_response_status with raw
    var redirects as int is calling petitio_response_redirect_count with raw
    var elapsed as f64 is calling petitio_response_elapsed with raw
    var protocol as HttpVersion is calling _http_version_from_code with (calling petitio_response_http_version with raw)
    var written as i64 is calling petitio_response_bytes_written with raw
    var response as Response is:
        status is status
        headers is headers
        body is body
        url is effective
        elapsed_sec is elapsed
        bytes_written is written
        http_version is protocol
        redirected is redirects > 0
        cookies is cookies
        cleared_cookies is expired
    return response

## The C request code for `HttpVersion` (0 = 1.1, 1 = ALPN, 2 = prior
## knowledge, 3 = 1.0). `Http3` has no request code; the builder rejects it.
weave _http_version_code with version as HttpVersion into int:
    return judge version:
        when Http10 -> 3
        when Http11 -> 0
        when Http2 -> 1
        when Http2PriorKnowledge -> 2
        when Http3 -> 0

## The `HttpVersion` for the C response code (0 = 1.0, 2 = 2, 4 = 3, rest = 1.1).
weave _http_version_from_code with code as int into HttpVersion:
    return judge code:
        when 0 -> HttpVersion.Http10
        when 2 -> HttpVersion.Http2
        when 4 -> HttpVersion.Http3
        else -> HttpVersion.Http11

## The C code for `AuthMode` (0 = none, 1 = Basic, 2 = Digest, 3 = any).
weave _auth_mode_code with mode as AuthMode into int:
    return judge mode:
        when NoAuth -> 0
        when BasicAuth -> 1
        when DigestAuth -> 2
        when AnyAuth -> 3

## An empty header map, for the helpers that take no overlay.
weave _no_headers into map of string to string:
    return map of string to string

## Builds and configures the C request, merging `overlay_headers` (session
## defaults, never overriding a request header) and `cookies` (one `Cookie`
## header). Returns NULL only on allocation failure; the caller owns the handle.
weave _build_handle with request as ref to Request, overlay_headers as ref to map of string to string, cookies as ref to map of string to string into ref to petitio_request:
    var handle as ref to petitio_request is calling petitio_request_new with request->url
    if calling ffi.is_null with handle:
        return handle

    calling petitio_request_set_method with handle, request->method
    calling petitio_request_set_http_version with handle, (calling _http_version_code with request->http_version)
    for name in request->headers:
        calling petitio_request_add_header with handle, name, (calling request->headers.get with name)
    for name in essence of overlay_headers:
        if not (calling request->headers.contains with name):
            calling petitio_request_add_header with handle, name, (calling overlay_headers.get with name)

    if not (calling request->headers.contains with "user-agent") and not (calling _has_key with overlay_headers, "user-agent"):
        calling petitio_request_add_header with handle, "User-Agent", PETITIO_DEFAULT_USER_AGENT

    if (request->bearer_token length) > 0 and not (calling request->headers.contains with "authorization") and not (calling _has_key with overlay_headers, "authorization"):
        var authorization as string is "Bearer {request->bearer_token}"
        calling petitio_request_add_header with handle, "Authorization", authorization
        banish authorization

    if (essence of cookies).len > 0 and not (calling request->headers.contains with "cookie"):
        var sb as StringBuilder is calling StringBuilder.new
        var first as bool is true
        for name in essence of cookies:
            if not first:
                calling sb.append with "; "
            set first is false
            calling sb.append with name
            calling sb.append_char with '='
            calling sb.append with (calling cookies.get with name)
        var cookie_header as string is calling sb.finish
        banish sb
        calling petitio_request_add_header with handle, "Cookie", cookie_header
        banish cookie_header

    if request->has_body:
        calling petitio_request_set_body with handle, request->body

    calling petitio_request_set_timeout with handle, (calling _seconds_to_ms with request->timeout_sec), (calling _seconds_to_ms with request->connect_timeout_sec)
    calling petitio_request_set_redirects with handle, (calling _flag with request->follow_redirects), (request->max_redirects to i64)
    calling petitio_request_set_verify_tls with handle, (calling _flag with request->verify_tls)
    calling petitio_request_set_max_body with handle, request->max_body_bytes
    if (request->basic_user length) > 0:
        calling petitio_request_set_auth_mode with handle, (calling _auth_mode_code with request->auth_mode)
        calling petitio_request_set_basic_auth with handle, request->basic_user, request->basic_password
    if (request->proxy length) > 0:
        calling petitio_request_set_proxy with handle, request->proxy, request->proxy_credentials
    for part in request->parts:
        calling petitio_request_add_form_field with handle, part.name, part.value, part.filename, part.content_type
    return handle

## Sends `request`, merging `overlay_headers` (session defaults, never
## overriding a request header) and `cookies` (as a `Cookie` header).
weave _perform with request as ref to Request, overlay_headers as ref to map of string to string, cookies as ref to map of string to string into result of Response to HttpError:
    var handle as ref to petitio_request is calling _build_handle with request, overlay_headers, cookies
    if calling ffi.is_null with handle:
        return calling err_of with (with OutOfMemory is 0)
    defer calling petitio_request_free with handle

    var raw as ref to petitio_response is calling petitio_request_perform with handle
    if calling ffi.is_null with raw:
        return calling err_of with (with OutOfMemory is 0)
    defer calling petitio_response_free with raw

    var code as int is calling petitio_response_error with raw
    if code != 0:
        var reason as string is calling petitio_response_error_message with raw
        var failure as HttpError is calling _error_from_code with code, reason, request
        banish reason
        return calling err_of with failure

    var response as Response is calling _response_from_c with raw, request
    return calling ok_of with response

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Cookies
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

## The name of the first `name=value` pair in a `Set-Cookie` value (owned).
weave _cookie_name with value as string into string:
    var raw as ref to frozen byte is bytes of value
    var n as int is value length
    var end as int is 0
    while end < n and (raw at end) != 61 and (raw at end) != 59:
        set end is end + 1
    if end == 0:
        return ""
    return calling scrolls.substring with value, 0, end

## The value of the first `name=value` pair in a `Set-Cookie` value (owned).
weave _cookie_value with value as string into string:
    var raw as ref to frozen byte is bytes of value
    var n as int is value length
    var equal as int is 0
    while equal < n and (raw at equal) != 61 and (raw at equal) != 59:
        set equal is equal + 1
    if equal >= n or (raw at equal) != 61:
        return ""
    var start as int is equal + 1
    var end as int is start
    while end < n and (raw at end) != 59:
        set end is end + 1
    while start < end and ((raw at start) == 32 or (raw at start) == 9):
        set start is start + 1
    while end > start and ((raw at (end - 1)) == 32 or (raw at (end - 1)) == 9):
        set end is end - 1
    return calling scrolls.substring with value, start, end

## `true` when a `Set-Cookie` value clears the cookie.
##
## A cookie is cleared when `Max-Age` is zero **or negative** (RFC 6265 §5.2.2
## makes every non-positive delta expire immediately) or, when there is no
## `Max-Age`, when its `Expires` date is in the past (see
## `_cookie_expired_by_date`). `Max-Age` wins over `Expires` (§5.3): a one-hour
## `Max-Age` keeps the cookie even if `Expires` points at 1970.
##
## The attribute is parsed as a number (`Max-Age=0`, `max-age=-1`), not by
## substring: `Max-Age=01` is a one-second cookie and must not clear anything.
weave _cookie_cleared with value as string into bool:
    var lower as string is calling scrolls.lower with value
    var at as int is calling scrolls.find with lower, "max-age="
    if at < 0:
        banish lower
        # No Max-Age: `Expires` decides (RFC 6265 §5.3 gives Max-Age priority).
        return calling _cookie_expired_by_date with value
    var i as int is at + 8
    var n as int is lower length
    var raw as ref to frozen byte is bytes of lower
    while i < n and ((raw at i) == 32 or (raw at i) == 9):
        set i is i + 1
    var negative as bool is false
    if i < n and (raw at i) == 45:
        set negative is true
        set i is i + 1
    var digits as int is 0
    var magnitude as i64 is 0
    while i < n:
        var b as int is (raw at i) to int
        if b < 48 or b > 57:
            break
        set magnitude is (magnitude * 10) + ((b - 48) to i64)
        set digits is digits + 1
        set i is i + 1
    banish lower
    if digits == 0:
        return calling _cookie_expired_by_date with value
    # Any non-positive Max-Age expires now. `magnitude` is the absolute value,
    # so the sign is the only thing that matters: `-1` must clear as well.
    if negative:
        return true
    return magnitude == 0

## `true` when the `Expires` attribute of a `Set-Cookie` value is in the past.
##
## The date is parsed by libcurl (`curl_getdate`), which accepts every format
## RFC 7231 allows. A missing or unparseable `Expires` does not expire anything:
## only an explicit date at or before "now" clears the cookie.
##
## ## Memoria
## Allocates one lowercase copy and one date substring, both released here.
weave _cookie_expired_by_date with value as string into bool:
    # The attribute *name* is case-insensitive, but the date value must keep
    # its original case: curl_getdate rejects lower-case day and month names.
    var at as int is calling _find_ci with value, "expires="
    if at < 0:
        return false
    var i as int is at + 8
    var n as int is value length
    var raw as ref to frozen byte is bytes of value
    while i < n and ((raw at i) == 32 or (raw at i) == 9):
        set i is i + 1
    var end as int is i
    while end < n and (raw at end) != 59:
        set end is end + 1
    var date as string is calling scrolls.substring with value, i, end
    var stamp as i64 is calling petitio_parse_http_date with date
    banish date
    if stamp < 0:
        return false
    var now as i64 is (calling chronicle.time) to i64
    return stamp <= now

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Sessions
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

enchanting Session:
    ## Creates an empty session: no default headers, no cookies.
    weave ritual new into Session:
        var headers as map of string to string is map of string to string
        var cookies as map of string to string is map of string to string
        return with _default_headers is headers, _cookies is cookies

    ## Sets a default header. A request that sets the same name overrides it.
    ##
    ## ## Panics
    ## When the name is not an RFC 7230 token, or either part contains CR/LF.
    weave set_header with name as string, value as string into void:
        calling _set_header with (sigil of self->_default_headers), name, value

    ## Removes a default header. Returns `true` when it was present.
    weave remove_header with name as string into bool:
        var key as string is calling scrolls.lower with name
        var removed as bool is calling _remove_owned with (sigil of self->_default_headers), key
        banish key
        return removed

    ## `true` when the session sets `name` as a default header.
    weave has_header with name as string into bool:
        var key as string is calling scrolls.lower with name
        var present as bool is calling _has_key with (sigil of self->_default_headers), key
        banish key
        return present

    ## Stores a cookie that every subsequent request sends.
    ##
    ## ## Panics
    ## When `name` is not an RFC 7230 token, or `name`/`value` contains ';' or a
    ## line break (either would corrupt the `Cookie` header).
    weave set_cookie with name as string, value as string into void:
        if not calling _is_token with name:
            calling spark.panic with "petitio: invalid cookie name '{name}'"
        if (calling _has_control_byte with value) or (calling scrolls.contains with value, ";"):
            calling spark.panic with "petitio: cookie '{name}' value contains ';', CR, LF or NUL"
        var key as string is calling _copy with name
        var stored as string is calling _copy with value
        calling _put_owned with (sigil of self->_cookies), key, stored

    ## Forgets one cookie. Returns `true` when it was present.
    weave remove_cookie with name as string into bool:
        return calling _remove_owned with (sigil of self->_cookies), name

    ## Forgets every cookie.
    ##
    ## ## Detalles
    ## The loop removes one cookie per iteration and verifies that the map
    ## actually shrank. If `_remove_owned` ever failed (a corrupt map, an OOM in
    ## a key copy), an unguarded `while` would spin forever; the loop breaks
    ## instead and leaves the remaining entries in place.
    weave clear_cookies into void:
        while self->_cookies.len > 0:
            var before as int is self->_cookies.len
            var victim as string is ""
            for name in self->_cookies:
                set victim is (calling _copy with name)
                break
            if (victim length) == 0:
                break
            var removed as bool is calling _remove_owned with (sigil of self->_cookies), victim
            banish victim
            if not removed or self->_cookies.len >= before:
                break

    ## The number of stored cookies.
    weave cookie_count into int:
        return self->_cookies.len

    ## `true` when the session stores `name`.
    weave has_cookie with name as string into bool:
        return calling self->_cookies.contains with name

    ## Sends `req` with the session's headers and cookies, and updates the
    ## cookie jar from the response.
    ##
    ## ## Detalles
    ## A header set on the request always wins over the session default (the
    ## merge is name-by-name). An explicit `Cookie` header on the request
    ## replaces the session's cookies for that call; the jar is still updated
    ## from the response.
    weave request with req as ref to Request into result of Response to HttpError:
        var outcome as result of Response to HttpError is calling _perform with req, (sigil of self->_default_headers), (sigil of self->_cookies)
        if not outcome.is_ok:
            return outcome
        var resp as Response is outcome.value
        for name in resp.cookies:
            var key as string is calling _copy with name
            var value as string is calling _copy with (calling resp.cookies.get with name)
            calling _put_owned with (sigil of self->_cookies), key, value
        for name in resp.cleared_cookies:
            calling _remove_owned with (sigil of self->_cookies), name
        return outcome

    ## `GET url` through the session.
    weave get with url as string into result of Response to HttpError:
        var req as Request is calling Request.new with "GET", url
        defer banish req
        return calling self.request with (sigil of req)

    ## `POST url` with a JSON body, through the session.
    weave post_json with url as string, v as json.JsonValue into result of Response to HttpError:
        var req as Request is calling Request.new with "POST", url
        defer banish req
        calling req.json_body with v
        return calling self.request with (sigil of req)

    ## `POST url` with a form-urlencoded body, through the session.
    weave post_form with url as string, fields as map of string to string into result of Response to HttpError:
        var req as Request is calling Request.new with "POST", url
        defer banish req
        calling req.form_body with fields
        return calling self.request with (sigil of req)

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# One-shot helpers (the `requests.get` / `requests.post` shape)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

## `GET url` with default settings.
##
## ## Memoria
## Returns an owned `Response`; `banish` it. The request is created and released
## inside the call.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## var r as result of Response to HttpError is calling petitio.get with "https://example.com"
## defer banish r
## if not r.is_ok:
##     return 1
## var resp as Response is r.value          # borrowed copy: do not banish
## calling spark.println_int with resp.status
## ```
weave get with url as string into result of Response to HttpError:
    var request as Request is calling Request.new with "GET", url
    defer banish request
    return calling request.send

## `HEAD url` with default settings.
weave head with url as string into result of Response to HttpError:
    var request as Request is calling Request.new with "HEAD", url
    defer banish request
    return calling request.send

## `DELETE url` with default settings.
weave delete with url as string into result of Response to HttpError:
    var request as Request is calling Request.new with "DELETE", url
    defer banish request
    return calling request.send

## `OPTIONS url` with default settings.
weave options with url as string into result of Response to HttpError:
    var request as Request is calling Request.new with "OPTIONS", url
    defer banish request
    return calling request.send

## `POST url` with an empty body.
weave post with url as string into result of Response to HttpError:
    var request as Request is calling Request.new with "POST", url
    defer banish request
    return calling request.send

## `POST url` with a JSON body.
weave post_json with url as string, v as json.JsonValue into result of Response to HttpError:
    var request as Request is calling Request.new with "POST", url
    defer banish request
    calling request.json_body with v
    return calling request.send

## `POST url` with a form-urlencoded body.
weave post_form with url as string, fields as map of string to string into result of Response to HttpError:
    var request as Request is calling Request.new with "POST", url
    defer banish request
    calling request.form_body with fields
    return calling request.send

## `PUT url` with a JSON body.
weave put_json with url as string, v as json.JsonValue into result of Response to HttpError:
    var request as Request is calling Request.new with "PUT", url
    defer banish request
    calling request.json_body with v
    return calling request.send

## `PATCH url` with a JSON body.
weave patch_json with url as string, v as json.JsonValue into result of Response to HttpError:
    var request as Request is calling Request.new with "PATCH", url
    defer banish request
    calling request.json_body with v
    return calling request.send

## `POST url` with a plain text body and an explicit content type.
weave post_text with url as string, body as string, content_type as string into result of Response to HttpError:
    var request as Request is calling Request.new with "POST", url
    defer banish request
    calling request.text_body with body
    calling request.header with "Content-Type", content_type
    return calling request.send

## The `User-Agent` this module sends when a request does not set one.
weave default_user_agent into string:
    return PETITIO_DEFAULT_USER_AGENT

## The libcurl runtime version this build links against (e.g. `"8.22.0"`).
##
## ## Retorno
## An owned version string; `banish` it. Useful in bug reports and in a startup
## banner that names the transport.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## var version as string is calling petitio.libcurl_version
## calling spark.println with version
## banish version
## ```
weave libcurl_version into string:
    return calling petitio_version

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tests (run with `pengu test --entry std/petitio.pengu`)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# These live inside the module because they exercise private helpers
# (`_cookie_cleared`, `_cookie_name`, `_is_token`, …) that are deliberately not
# exported. The public, network-free behaviour is covered by
# `tests/stdlib/test_petitio.py` and the conformance corpus; the live half lives
# in `tests/compat/test_petitio_vs_requests.py`.

## Panics with `label` when `cond` is false.
weave _expect with cond as bool, label as string into void:
    if not cond:
        calling spark.panic with "petitio test failed: {label}"

## Panics with `label` when `actual != expected`.
weave _expect_int with actual as int, expected as int, label as string into void:
    if actual != expected:
        calling spark.panic with "petitio test failed: {label}: {actual} != {expected}"

## Panics with `label` when the two strings differ.
weave _expect_str with actual as string, expected as string, label as string into void:
    if (calling scrolls.compare with actual, expected) != 0:
        calling spark.panic with "petitio test failed: {label}: '{actual}' != '{expected}'"

test "Max-Age zero and negative clear the cookie":
    calling _expect with (calling _cookie_cleared with "sid=x; Max-Age=0"), "Max-Age=0"
    calling _expect with (calling _cookie_cleared with "sid=x; Max-Age=-1"), "Max-Age=-1"
    calling _expect with (calling _cookie_cleared with "sid=x; Max-Age=-0"), "Max-Age=-0"
    calling _expect with (calling _cookie_cleared with "sid=x; max-age=-999"), "negative lower-case"

test "a positive Max-Age keeps the cookie":
    calling _expect with not (calling _cookie_cleared with "sid=x; Max-Age=1"), "Max-Age=1"
    calling _expect with not (calling _cookie_cleared with "sid=x; Max-Age=01"), "Max-Age=01"
    calling _expect with not (calling _cookie_cleared with "sid=x; Max-Age=3600"), "Max-Age=3600"

test "a cookie without Max-Age or Expires stays":
    calling _expect with not (calling _cookie_cleared with "sid=x; Path=/"), "plain cookie"
    calling _expect with not (calling _cookie_cleared with "sid=x; Max-Age=abc"), "unparseable Max-Age"

test "Expires in the past clears the cookie":
    calling _expect with (calling _cookie_cleared with "sid=x; Expires=Thu, 01 Jan 1970 00:00:00 GMT"), "past Expires"

test "Expires in the future keeps the cookie":
    calling _expect with not (calling _cookie_cleared with "sid=x; Expires=Thu, 01 Jan 2099 00:00:00 GMT"), "future Expires"

test "Max-Age wins over Expires (RFC 6265 5.3)":
    calling _expect with not (calling _cookie_cleared with "sid=x; Max-Age=3600; Expires=Thu, 01 Jan 1970 00:00:00 GMT"), "positive Max-Age beats past Expires"
    calling _expect with (calling _cookie_cleared with "sid=x; Max-Age=0; Expires=Thu, 01 Jan 2099 00:00:00 GMT"), "zero Max-Age beats future Expires"

test "an unparseable Expires does not clear":
    calling _expect with not (calling _cookie_cleared with "sid=x; Expires=not-a-date"), "garbage Expires"

test "cookie name/value extraction":
    var name0 as string is calling _cookie_name with "sid=abc123; Path=/; HttpOnly"
    calling _expect_str with name0, "sid", "cookie name"
    banish name0
    var value0 as string is calling _cookie_value with "sid=abc123; Path=/; HttpOnly"
    calling _expect_str with value0, "abc123", "cookie value"
    banish value0
    var empty_name as string is calling _cookie_name with "=oops"
    calling _expect_int with (empty_name length), 0, "empty cookie name"
    banish empty_name
    var spaced as string is calling _cookie_value with "k=  padded value ; Path=/"
    calling _expect_str with spaced, "padded value", "trimmed cookie value"
    banish spaced

test "url_encode and url_decode round-trip":
    var encoded as string is calling url_encode with "a b&ñ"
    calling _expect_str with encoded, "a%20b%26%C3%B1", "encoded"
    var decoded as string is calling url_decode with encoded
    calling _expect_str with decoded, "a b&ñ", "round trip"
    banish decoded
    banish encoded
    var plus as string is calling url_decode with "a+b"
    calling _expect_str with plus, "a+b", "plus is not a space"
    banish plus
    var broken as string is calling url_decode with "%ZZ%2"
    calling _expect_str with broken, "%ZZ%2", "malformed escapes preserved"
    banish broken

test "build_query_string sorts and encodes":
    var params as map of string to string is map of string to string
    calling params.put with "z", "1"
    calling params.put with "a", "2 3"
    var query as string is calling build_query_string with params
    calling _expect_str with query, "a=2%203&z=1", "sorted query"
    banish query
    banish params

test "parse_url splits an absolute URL":
    var parsed as result of UrlParts to string is calling parse_url with "https://u:p@h:99/a?b=1#c"
    calling _expect with parsed.is_ok, "parse_url ok"
    if parsed.is_ok:
        var parts as UrlParts is parsed.value
        calling _expect_str with parts.scheme, "https", "scheme"
        calling _expect_str with parts.userinfo, "u:p", "userinfo"
        calling _expect_str with parts.host, "h", "host"
        calling _expect_int with parts.port, 99, "port"
        calling _expect_str with parts.path, "/a", "path"
        calling _expect_str with parts.query, "b=1", "query"
        calling _expect_str with parts.fragment, "c", "fragment"
    banish parsed
    var bad as result of UrlParts to string is calling parse_url with "nope"
    calling _expect with not bad.is_ok, "parse_url rejects a relative URL"
    banish bad

test "control bytes and tokens":
    calling _expect with (calling _has_control_byte with "a\rb"), "CR"
    calling _expect with (calling _has_control_byte with "a\nb"), "LF"
    # A NUL literal cannot be built here: string literals are NUL-terminated at
    # the C boundary. The NUL branch stays as defence in depth for strings that
    # arrive through `std.ffi.string_from_bytes`.
    calling _expect with not (calling _has_control_byte with "plain value"), "plain"
    calling _expect with (calling _is_token with "GET"), "token"
    calling _expect with (calling _is_token with "X-Custom"), "token with dash"
    calling _expect with not (calling _is_token with "bad name"), "space is not a token"
    calling _expect with not (calling _is_token with ""), "empty is not a token"

test "Request defaults and header replacement":
    var req as Request is calling Request.new with "get", "https://example.com/"
    calling _expect_str with req.method, "GET", "method upper-cased"
    calling _expect with req.follow_redirects, "redirects on"
    calling _expect_int with req.max_redirects, PETITIO_DEFAULT_MAX_REDIRECTS, "redirect limit"
    calling _expect with req.verify_tls, "TLS on"
    calling _expect with not req.has_body, "no body"
    calling req.header with "Content-Type", "text/plain"
    calling req.header with "content-TYPE", "application/json"
    calling _expect_int with req.headers.len, 1, "case-insensitive replacement"
    var ctype as string is calling req.headers.get with "content-type"
    calling _expect_str with ctype, "application/json", "last value wins"
    calling _expect with (calling req.has_header with "CONTENT-TYPE"), "has_header is CI"
    banish req

test "http_version defaults to HTTP/1.1 and is settable":
    var req as Request is calling Request.new with "GET", "https://example.com/"
    calling _expect_int with (calling _http_version_code with req.http_version), 0, "default version"
    calling req.http_version with HttpVersion.Http2
    calling _expect_int with (calling _http_version_code with req.http_version), 1, "ALPN code"
    calling req.http_version with HttpVersion.Http2PriorKnowledge
    calling _expect_int with (calling _http_version_code with req.http_version), 2, "prior-knowledge code"
    calling req.http_version with HttpVersion.Http10
    calling _expect_int with (calling _http_version_code with req.http_version), 3, "HTTP/1.0 code"
    banish req

test "the response protocol code maps back to an HttpVersion":
    var v10 as HttpVersion is calling _http_version_from_code with 0
    calling _expect_int with (calling _http_version_code with v10), 3, "1.0 round trip"
    var v11 as HttpVersion is calling _http_version_from_code with 1
    calling _expect_int with (calling _http_version_code with v11), 0, "1.1 round trip"
    var v2 as HttpVersion is calling _http_version_from_code with 2
    calling _expect_int with (calling _http_version_code with v2), 1, "2 round trip"
    var v3 as HttpVersion is calling _http_version_from_code with 4
    if v3 != HttpVersion.Http3:
        calling spark.panic with "petitio test failed: HTTP/3 mapping"

test "authentication modes are selected by their builders":
    var req as Request is calling Request.new with "GET", "https://example.com/"
    calling _expect_int with (calling _auth_mode_code with req.auth_mode), 0, "no auth by default"
    calling req.auth_basic with "u", "p"
    calling _expect_int with (calling _auth_mode_code with req.auth_mode), 1, "basic"
    calling req.auth_digest with "u", "p"
    calling _expect_int with (calling _auth_mode_code with req.auth_mode), 2, "digest"
    calling req.auth_any with "u", "p"
    calling _expect_int with (calling _auth_mode_code with req.auth_mode), 3, "any"
    calling _expect_str with req.basic_user, "u", "user stored"
    calling _expect_str with req.basic_password, "p", "password stored"
    banish req

test "socks_proxy prefixes socks5h and keeps an explicit scheme":
    var req as Request is calling Request.new with "GET", "https://example.com/"
    calling req.socks_proxy with "127.0.0.1:1080", ""
    calling _expect_str with req.proxy, "socks5h://127.0.0.1:1080", "socks5h prefix"
    calling req.socks_proxy with "socks5://127.0.0.1:1080", ""
    calling _expect_str with req.proxy, "socks5://127.0.0.1:1080", "explicit scheme kept"
    calling req.socks_proxy with "socks5h://127.0.0.1:1080", "u:p"
    calling _expect_str with req.proxy, "socks5h://127.0.0.1:1080", "socks5h kept"
    calling _expect_str with req.proxy_credentials, "u:p", "credentials kept"
    banish req

test "streaming error variants carry a message":
    var io_error as HttpError is with IoError is "cannot open output file: /nope"
    var io_message as string is calling io_error.message
    calling _expect_str with io_message, "I/O error: cannot open output file: /nope", "io message"
    banish io_message
    banish io_error
    var cancelled as HttpError is Cancelled
    var cancelled_message as string is calling cancelled.message
    calling _expect_str with cancelled_message, "transfer cancelled by callback", "cancelled message"
    banish cancelled_message
    banish cancelled

test "Session cookie jar operations":
    var session as Session is calling Session.new
    calling session.set_cookie with "sid", "abc"
    calling _expect_int with (calling session.cookie_count), 1, "one cookie"
    calling _expect with (calling session.has_cookie with "sid"), "has sid"
    var removed as bool is calling session.remove_cookie with "sid"
    calling _expect with removed, "remove_cookie"
    calling _expect_int with (calling session.cookie_count), 0, "empty jar"
    calling session.set_cookie with "a", "1"
    calling session.set_cookie with "b", "2"
    calling session.clear_cookies
    calling _expect_int with (calling session.cookie_count), 0, "clear_cookies"
    banish session

test "take_response and take_error leave the result banish-safe":
    var box as result of Response to HttpError is calling ok_of with (calling _empty_response)
    var moved as Response is calling take_response with (sigil of box)
    calling _expect_int with moved.status, 0, "moved status"
    banish moved
    banish box                          # must be a no-op, not a double free

    var err_box as result of Response to HttpError is calling err_of with (with TlsError is "bad")
    var error_value as HttpError is calling take_error with (sigil of err_box)
    var message as string is calling error_value.message
    calling _expect_str with message, "TLS error: bad", "moved error message"
    banish message
    banish error_value
    banish err_box                      # must be a no-op

## A zeroed `Response`, used by the move tests.
weave _empty_response into Response:
    var headers as map of string to string is map of string to string
    var cookies as map of string to string is map of string to string
    var cleared as list of string is list of string
    var response as Response is:
        status is 0
        headers is headers
        body is ""
        url is ""
        elapsed_sec is 0.0
        bytes_written is 0
        http_version is HttpVersion.Http11
        redirected is false
        cookies is cookies
        cleared_cookies is cleared
    return response
